    "name":  "Alcoholic hepatitis without ascites",
    "module":  "hepatobiliary",
    "category":  "disease",
    "description":  "Alcoholic hepatitis is an acute inflammatory condition of the liver caused by sustained heavy alcohol consumption, typically more than 8–10 standard drinks per day for at least 10 years. It presents with rapid-onset jaundice, right upper quadrant pain, fever, and elevated liver enzymes (predominantly AST:ALT ratio \u003e2:1). Severe cases (Maddrey discriminant function ≥32) carry significant 28-day mortality and may warrant corticosteroid therapy. It must be distinguished from cirrhosis and other causes of hepatitis.",
